    "humanReview": "Qualitative user approval; numeric ratings remain unmeasured.",
    "entrance": "Lower west bank beneath the loaded carriage.",
    "exit": "Raised eastern gallery crossed by three sun shafts.",
    "solution": "Catch the freight ring and reel in below the low roof. The lantern fits above the carriage; the knight does not. As the train emerges, pay out and pump toward its cargo edge. Jump free during the rising outward swing, dash straight up beside the platform, and hold Grab after starting the dash. The moving lantern ends the burst while retaining its full upward speed. Steer right on the carrying glide and keep the pack above the knight through the sun shafts.",
    "nearestExisting": "B38 loads a carriage and retrieves its cargo from a stationary dock. Run 4 B43 also has a stationary pickup. Here the freight never parks its cargo: rope length, a live edge rendezvous, and the new velocity-preserving catch replace docking. The wide receiving shelf keeps the final landing forgiving.",
    "novelty": "The moving platform simultaneously carries the required shade above the route and the knight below it. Departure changes attachment from its rope to its moving cargo, and the act of catching supplies the usable vertical continuation.",
    "designNotes": "The roof has exactly cargo clearance, so riding on top is not the intended passage. The far ledge is broad and the catch is possible across several nearby swing/ride/release timings. Grab can be held shortly after starting the upward dash; it does not demand one particular catch frame. No hidden technique-name gate.",
